# Markdown: the inline marks: bold, italic, underline, strikethrough, code, links, styled runs and escapes.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Markdown · Inline formatting
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: price
			Typography:
				Color: #A12A1E
				Bold: true
		For style: brand
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Serif
				Italic: true
	Section:
		Text: Markdown
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Inline formatting
		Paragraph: Inside a `Markdown` the marks of a line work as in `Markup: markdown`. The code goes in the `Code font` of the `Typography`, a link is underlined and `[text]{name}` takes the look of the `For style: name` rule. A backslash writes a mark as it is.
			Style: intro
		Markdown:
			Content >>
				**Bold**, *italic* and ***both***. ++Underlined++ and ~~struck through~~.

				The command `mvn test` runs the tests, in the code font.

				The [website](https://stxt.dev) and the [section on prices](#prices) are links.

				A subscription to [The Gazette]{brand} costs [€12.50]{price} a month.

				Written as they are: \*not italic\*, \[not a link\] and \`not code\`.

				## Prices {#prices}

				The prices include VAT.
